Restore CAMERA_PARAMETERS_EXTRA_{C,H} hooks in frameworks/av (lineage-15.1)

Target tree: frameworks/av (LineageOS lineage-15.1).

Why: the Samsung blob chain of GT-I8150 (ancora) imports a large set of
Samsung/Qualcomm CameraParameters extensions (KEY_ISO_MODE, KEY_TOUCH_*,
ISO_*, VIDEO_HFR_*, get/setTouchIndex*, getPreviewFrameRateMode, ...).
cm-13.0's frameworks/av carried guarded CAMERA_PARAMETERS_EXTRA_C / _H hooks
in camera/CameraParameters.cpp and camera/include/camera/CameraParameters.h,
plus a commented-out default template include/camera/CameraParametersExtra.h
that device trees override.  Lineage-15.1 dropped the hook in the class
header.  The cpp-side hook is unnecessary here because our device tree ships
the whole CameraParameters implementation itself via
TARGET_SPECIFIC_CAMERA_PARAMETER_LIBRARY -> libcamera_parameters_ancora
(see device/samsung/ancora/camera/camera_parameters/).

This patch restores only the header-side hook, guarded, so it is a no-op for
every other LineageOS 15.1 build; it lets libcamera_parameters_ancora's copy
of CameraParameters.cpp compile with the Samsung extensions declared inside
the class (expanded from "CameraParametersExtra.h", which that copy includes
FIRST, before <camera/CameraParameters.h>).

Apply with:
    cd frameworks/av && git apply \
        device/samsung/ancora/patches/frameworks-av-15.1-camera-params-extra.patch

--- a/camera/include/camera/CameraParameters.h
+++ b/camera/include/camera/CameraParameters.h
@@ -682,7 +682,12 @@
     static const char LIGHTFX_LOWLIGHT[];
     // High-dynamic range mode
     static const char LIGHTFX_HDR[];
 
+#ifdef CAMERA_PARAMETERS_EXTRA_H
+CAMERA_PARAMETERS_EXTRA_H
+#endif
+
     /**
      * Returns the the supported preview formats as an enum given in graphics.h
      * corrsponding to the format given in the input string or -1 if no such
